  "result": "Archiving a project now only archives its issues that are still live. I haven't run the tests or the app.\n\nThe fix is in `archiveIssuesForProject` in `src/server/repositories/issue-repository.ts`, which now skips issues that already have an archive date. That covers each part of the report:\n\n- **Older archive dates:** the 3 issues archived by hand keep their original archive date, so the retention sweep sees the right one.\n- **Reported count:** the function returns the number of rows it actually changed, so the audit-log entry would say 9 instead of 12.\n- **Usage meter:** the usage listener subtracts that same count, so the meter drops by 9 and stays equal to a recount of live issues. It should no longer go negative.\n- **Other projects:** the update is still limited to the one project and workspace, so nothing else is touched.\n\nI didn't change the event, activity or usage code, since they already use the returned count.",
